trix}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535495 17592186045443 true] [17592186423271 1074 "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535495 17592186045443 false] [17592186423271 1074 "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139535495 17592186045443 true] [17592186423355 1071 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139535495 17592186045443 false] [17592186423355 1071 "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe matrix of t